  "coverage": "Denmark: five regions and 98 municipalities (DAGI, July 2026 interior boundaries; retained atlas national silhouette), with Christiansø kept outside the municipal and regional hierarchy. Greenland: five municipalities and the Northeast Greenland National Park (2020 geoBoundaries outline). Faroe Islands: all 29 municipalities from Umhvørvisstovan, May 2026. Greenland and the Faroe Islands open directly at their own location. The Danish regional merger takes effect in 2027 and is not applied early.",
  "processing": "Danish municipal interiors and parishes share one DAGI topology simplified at 0.00003 degrees; regions dissolve from the same municipalities. The retained atlas national silhouette and coastal fallback preserve the international frontier. Ordinary internal edges have one visible owner; selected outlines use the same screen-space detail. Population, economy and North Atlantic territory geometry remain unchanged.",
